!!! 04-paragraphs.matrix
!!! Declarations, named arguments, mutable parameters, variadics, recursion
!!! and paragraph values.
!!!
!!! The universal declaration shape is:
!!!     <modifiers> <name> <clauses...> begin <kind>
!!!         ...
!!!     end <kind>
!!! "returns" terminates the parameter list. Omitting it means
!!! "returns nothing".

book tour.functions

!!! Two parameters, separated by a comma.
add_two receives left as number, right as number returns number begin paragraph
    give left plus right
end paragraph

!!! The same declaration written with the draft's "and". It is accepted
!!! between parameter declarations only, because each item there has the
!!! fixed shape <name> as <type>. Elsewhere "and" is boolean conjunction.
add_three receives a as number and b as number and c as number returns number begin paragraph
    give a plus b plus c
end paragraph

!!! No result. "returns nothing" may be written or omitted.
announce receives message as text begin paragraph
    say message
end paragraph

!!! No parameters.
answer returns number begin paragraph
    give 42
end paragraph

!!! A mutable parameter is the callee's own binding. It does not mutate the
!!! caller's scalar, exactly as Ny's "mut" parameter does not.
!!! The older "variable amount" spelling remains a parameter alias.
increment_local receives mutable amount as number returns number begin paragraph
    set amount to amount plus 1
    give amount
end paragraph

!!! Ordinary recursion.
factorial receives count as number returns number begin paragraph
    when count is at most 1 then
        give 1
    end when
    give count times (factorial with count being count minus 1)
end paragraph

!!! A trailing variadic collects the remaining arguments into an array.
sum_all receives more values as number returns number begin paragraph
    variable total as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than (the length of values)
        set total to total plus (values at index)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph

!!! A default is retained in the syntax tree and is restricted to a literal
!!! atom. Ny currently rejects omitted arguments at the call site, so every
!!! caller must still pass every parameter.
retry receives attempts as number defaulting to 3 returns number begin paragraph
    give attempts
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph

    !!! Named arguments cannot be mis-ordered. They lower to positional NIL
    !!! arguments in declaration order. Because Ny has no overload
    !!! resolution, argument names are checked against the one declaration
    !!! and never select between candidates.
    say add_two with left being 1, right being 2
    say add_two with right being 2, left being 1
    say add_three with a being 1, b being 2, c being 3

    !!! A zero-argument call is still syntactically a call.
    say answer with nothing
    evaluate announce with message being "dispatching"

    value original as number is 5
    say increment_local with amount being original
    say original                                 !!! still 5

    say factorial with count being 5
    !!! A variadic tail is introduced by "more", mirroring "receives more
    !!! values as integer" in the declaration, so a trailing list of values is
    !!! never confusable with further named arguments.
    say sum_all with nothing                     !!! zero variadic arguments
    say sum_all with more 1, 2, 3, 4
    say retry with attempts being 5

    !!! A named paragraph value. Captures are rejected, so a paragraph value is
    !!! a reference to a declared function. Paragraph values and anonymous
    !!! functions are covered on interpreted routes only: native indirect
    !!! calls are not implemented.
    value operation is the paragraph add_two
    say operation with left being 20, right being 22

    !!! An anonymous paragraph. Noncapturing only; it may not read "original".
    value doubler is anonymous receives n as number returns number begin paragraph
        give n times 2
    end paragraph
    say doubler with n being 21

    give 0
end paragraph
